#
# Log why a subkey-only import was refused. Patch 21 accepts the FAILURE
# that ends the passphrase edit of a key whose primary secret is a stub
# only after checking the key, and refuses otherwise. One such refusal
# in CI could not be explained afterwards (#187): the only message was
# "Changing the key passphrase failed" or one of its two siblings, which
# says neither which secret was refused nor what the check saw. Each
# refusal now logs what it rested on: the listing the check used beside
# one taken at that moment and the key files present; the secret that
# does not accept the new passphrase, or still accepts the old; a
# verifying agent that gave neither answer, with its exit status and
# diagnostics; and how long the edit session took and which passphrase
# answered each of its prompts. No passphrase or key material is
# logged, and no check changes: what was refused is still refused. See
# patches/README.md.
#
